# What the build may read: everything is excluded, then the few files the Dockerfile copies are let back in. A new
# file never reaches the daemon or the image by accident, in particular none of the git-ignored ones that hold secrets
# or real data (.env, hlp.toml, users.json, audit.log, snapshots/).
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!homelab_probe
!docs/schemas

# Even inside what was let in: no secret, no state, no cache, wherever it is.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/hlp.toml
**/users.json*
**/audit.log*
**/snapshots
**/certs
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/.git
